---
// Compare tab: one prompt, two arms, one shared seed — the same graph
// scripts/ab_modelo.py drives, so a run here lines up with the table in
// docs/levers-and-dead-ends.md.
---

<main id="view-compare" hidden>
  <form class="panel" id="compare-form">
    <label for="c_prompt">Prompt <span class="hint">(both arms)</span></label>
    <textarea id="c_prompt" required>1girl, solo, long red hair, looking at viewer, standing</textarea>

    <label for="c_negative">Negative <span class="hint">(blank = per-family default)</span></label>
    <textarea id="c_negative" style="min-height:52px"></textarea>

    <div class="row">
      <div>
        <label for="c_arm_a">Arm A</label>
        <select id="c_arm_a"></select>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="c_arm_b">Arm B</label>
        <select id="c_arm_b"></select>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="armcfg" id="c_cfg_a"></div>
    <div class="armcfg" id="c_cfg_b"></div>

    <label for="c_seed">Seed <span class="hint">(shared by both; blank = random)</span></label>
    <input id="c_seed" type="number" placeholder="random" />

    <div class="row">
      <div><label for="c_width">Width</label><input id="c_width" type="number" value="1024" step="64" min="256" /></div>
      <div><label for="c_height">Height</label><input id="c_height" type="number" value="1024" step="64" min="256" /></div>
    </div>

    <details>
      <summary>Override both arms</summary>
      <div class="row">
        <div><label for="c_steps">Steps</label><input id="c_steps" type="number" placeholder="per arm" /></div>
        <div><label for="c_cfg">CFG</label><input id="c_cfg" type="number" step="0.5" placeholder="per arm" /></div>
      </div>
      <label for="c_anima_model">Anima UNET</label>
      <input id="c_anima_model" type="text" />
      <p class="note">Left blank each arm uses its own recommended sampler,
      scheduler, steps and cfg &mdash; which is what makes the run comparable
      with the table in <code>docs/levers-and-dead-ends.md</code>. Forcing a
      shared value measures something else.</p>
    </details>

    <button id="compare-go" type="submit">Render both</button>
    <p class="note">Bare text2img, no scene, no face pass, no upscale &mdash; the
    same graph <code>scripts/ab_modelo.py</code> uses. One worker and one GPU
    means the arms run <b>in series</b>; across families ComfyUI reloads ~5 GB
    of model between them, so the second image lands ~1 min later.</p>
  </form>

  <section>
    <div class="sides">
      <div class="side panel" id="side-A"></div>
      <div class="side panel" id="side-B"></div>
    </div>
    <div id="compare-err" class="err" style="margin-top:12px"></div>
  </section>
</main>
